     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">\r\nThere’s no bug. The exonic targets you have are overlapping. They should not.\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Yuchao</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>ref=ranges(ref_qc[seqnames(ref_qc)==&#39;chr14&#39;])</div>\r\n<div>countOverlaps(ref,ref)</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On Jan 17, 2019, at 9:27 AM, Janka Puterová &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">iput...@fit.vutbr.cz</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\nYes, the data comes from the same sample:<span> </span>MM-ARK-07-418-aPC. I am sending you a link to all output data I saved during CODEX2 analysis as well as RData workspaces.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/nhyewjnbiytxo7w/codex_results.tar.gz?dl=0\" style=\"color:rgb(4,122,198);text-decoration:underline;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/nhyewjnbiytxo7w/codex_results.tar.gz?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243839431000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2FNSQLSCtn_jvA_7olZvY5\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/nhyewjnbiytxo7w/codex_results.tar.gz?dl=0</a></div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\nPlease, see below the description of files:</div>\r\n<ul style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none\">\r\n<li>MM_copynumbers.csv - resulting copynumbers</li><li>MM_coverage.csv - raw read depth (coverageObj)</li><li>MM_qcmat.csv - quality control (qcmat)</li><li>MM_copynumbers.Rdata - contains everything from preprocessing to running codex2 from the demo until codeline N &lt;-<span style=\"line-height:1.57143em\"><span> </span></span><span style=\"line-height:1.57143em\">apply</span>(<span style=\"line-height:1.57143em\">apply</span>(Y.nonzero,<span> </span><span style=\"line-height:1.57143em\">2</span>,\r\n function(x){x/pseudo.sample}),<span> </span><span style=\"line-height:1.57143em\">2</span>, median) </li><li>MM_workspace.RData - contain everything from Running CODEX2 with negative control samples to end of analysis</li></ul>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\nJanka</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:1.57143em;font-family:gotham,helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgb(56,56,56);font-variant-ligatures:normal\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none\">\r\nOn 16.01.2019 17:07, Jiang, Yuchao wrote:<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Hi Janka,<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Are these from the same sample? Can you send me the normalized data and raw read count data, as well as the ref_qc object and I will take a look?<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Yuchao<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border-style:solid none none;border-top-width:1pt;border-top-color:rgb(225,225,225);padding:3pt 0in 0in\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:windowtext\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:windowtext\"><span> </span>Janka\r\n Puterová<span> </span><a href style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;iput...@fit.vutbr.cz&gt;</a><span> </span><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b><span> </span>Wednesday, January 16, 2019 9:58 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b><span> </span>Jiang, Yuchao<span> </span><a href style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;yuc...@email.unc.edu&gt;</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b><span> </span>CODEX2 weird behavior<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nDear Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nI am using your tool CODEX2 for copynumber detection in matched normal-tumor samples. I used it on three datasets which altogether contained 58 patients (116 samples). All samples are fine except one, where I have found overlapping copy number regions (see\r\n the data bellow, bold rows). Is this expected behavior of the tool or is it some kind of bug? Which copy number should I take into consideration in this case?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<b>chr14 105864160 105895670 0.291</b><br>\r\nchr14 105844713 105860243 1.325<br>\r\nchr14 105860253 105863349 3.015<br>\r\nchr14 106680602 106875071 2.76<br>\r\nchr14 105837032 105845677 1.611<br>\r\nchr14 68861792 68925696 2.566<br>\r\n<b>chr14 105863675 105864196 1.096</b><br>\r\nchr14 49643541 49655819 2.487<br>\r\nchr14 91338016 91462247 1.543<br>\r\nchr14 94045775 94227385 1.712<br>\r\nchr14 64024279 64141501 2.176<br>\r\nchr15 51958661 51958906 0.874<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nThank you very much for your answer.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nYours sincerely,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nJanka Puterova<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\nBioinformatician/PhD student at Brno University of Technology, Czechia<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-left:0in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration:none\">\r\n<br>\r\n<table style=\"border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(211,212,222)\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width:55px;padding-top:18px\"><a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=link&amp;utm_campaign=sig-email&amp;utm_content=emailclient\" style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dlink%26utm_campaign%3Dsig-email%26utm_content%3Demailclient&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243839431000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37JuXZ8kjp9W11RUghwRq6\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/IAkhl6EbYbQYD9J_1Dc6N_HPU5Z488DnGcKcnWpOKuYmchAYVxkuaNLcLza-a4lma2s9ti4CdivC6ngcOg6DxsKIfQSj1jUPE23T-RPW6SSIBxsEZEVz9o7f4AeRul4zwq6JNmxjsa05TVZzHfERYYI-=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ipmcdn.avast.com/images/icons/icon-envelope-tick-round-orange-animated-no-repeat-v1.gif\" alt=\"\" width=\"46\" height=\"29\" style=\"width:46px;min-height:29px\"></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"width